BUG-38, second set: three more superlinear costs in documents with thousands of anchored
objects, found with a named CPU profile of the import of 8,000 generated shapes (after the
first set) and of cma's layout. All exact; not WASM-specific.

1. SdrCustomShapeGeometryItem is pooled through HashedItemInstanceManager
   (svx/source/items/customshapeitem.cxx, include/svx/sdasitm.hxx). It had no instance
   manager, so the default one found an equal item by a linear search with operator== over
   every geometry in the document: 4.5 s of a 23.6 s import. hashCode() returns the item's
   own content hash (comphelper::anyToHash of the property sequence, which operator== already
   compares before the sequences), or 0 when that hash is unusable; so equal items hash equal
   by construction, and the unusable ones are told apart by operator== as before.
2. DelFlyInRange (sw/source/core/doc/docedt.cxx) visits only the formats anchored on the
   range's own nodes (SwNode::GetAnchoredFlys), in the order of the full scan (descending
   table position), instead of every format in the document on every call: the import's
   DeleteAndJoin (once per text box) made it O(n^2), 3.0 s of the import. Every branch of
   IsSelectFrameAnchoredAtPara / IsDestroyFrameAnchoredAtChar bounds the anchor node by the
   range's, so the candidates are a superset of what the scan selects; the same predicate
   decides. A candidate deleted along the way is skipped. The full scan, unchanged, remains
   for a range spanning more nodes than there are formats.
3. SwViewShellImp::AddPendingLOKInvalidation de-duplicated each invalidation with a linear
   std::find over all pending ones (O(n^2): 6 s of cma's layout). A hash set alongside the
   vector now does the check; the vector, its order and its contents are the same, so
   nothing downstream sees a difference.

Documents module only for now.

